      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785445701398,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "using cryptography based on elliptic curves \nand thus the aim is to provide more security to the existing elliptic curve based cryptography we change our \nsystem towards cryptography based on lattice and introduce errors in multiple dimension \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "using cryptography based on elliptic curves \nand thus the aim is to provide more security to the existing elliptic curve based cryptography we change our \nsystem towards cryptography based on lattice and introduce errors in multiple dimension \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HozpxjORUl53dW61brbmh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -102.30930670142766,
      "y": 51390.06672663921,
      "width": 1059.23974609375,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bEp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2067872723,
      "version": 107,
      "versionNonce": 1084964733,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785445687038,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "and now client has finished and it enters sending the application data \nencrypted with the cipher spec that has been chosen between the\nserver and client there are much more functions but what I have created is a\nhigh level jist of what's going on under the hood of the World how data is \nencrypted and travelled between authenticated parties",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "and now client has finished and it enters sending the application data \nencrypted with the cipher spec that has been chosen between the\nserver and client there are much more functions but what I have created is a\nhigh level jist of what's going on under the hood of the World how data is \nencrypted and travelled between authenticated parties",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ECNOkXh4S2lGKk8PaM9A4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -714.2332430934143,
      "y": 51882.05162691806,
      "width": 2542.10400390625,
      "height": 252.24013220540658,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
