      "index": "bEr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 232514835,
      "version": 725,
      "versionNonce": 203815315,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785445997180,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q. What functions to change and what things to keep in mind while integrating MLDSA with mbed-TLS?\nSo, what I have thought of is I will backtrack from the end where the last actual function is used for signing and verifying the \nmessage and generating the hash using ECDSA, and I will backtrack from that file to the root file where I think that the \nbranch for MLDSA and ECDSA can be separated so what I thought of to do this is mentioned below, there may be discrepancies\nbut this is what I thought of while doing it ->",
      "fontSize": 40.358421152865056,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q. What functions to change and what things to keep in mind while integrating MLDSA with mbed-TLS?\nSo, what I have thought of is I will backtrack from the end where the last actual function is used for signing and verifying the \nmessage and generating the hash using ECDSA, and I will backtrack from that file to the root file where I think that the \nbranch for MLDSA and ECDSA can be separated so what I thought of to do this is mentioned below, there may be discrepancies\nbut this is what I thought of while doing it ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HGUrYylvvUjSGBpbgGtav",
